From: juanan <juanan@test.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:14:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] T5: add backup and restore of weights and validation
 history

- Weights are backed up as a child of each criterion, so they are copied
  with or without user data.
- The validation history is backed up as a child of each grading
  instance (only with user data), annotating teacher and validator as
  users. The persistent technical fields are regenerated on restore.
- Restore remaps instance, criterion, levels, graded item (through the
  grading manager API and the activity item mapping) and users, and saves
  through the persistents. Rows whose criterion or item cannot be mapped
  are skipped; unmapped users are left empty so the grade stays locked.
- Old backups restore with weight 1 and no validation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
